A||||1||engine18||Squealing Noise||||8||
Z||000000||engine18||02-10-2000||02:50 PM||||I have a 84 manual 2m4, with no air condition.  During startup and in neutral, I have a load squealing sounds from engine.  After a minute of driving, the squealing will stop......but will return at stop lights.  Is it the waterpump???? Or the tension of belt.  I recently install a drivebelt by instruction of the Haynes manual.  Thanks for any technical suggestions....||||reg||8
Z||000001||kidzwheelz||02-10-2000||02:59 PM||||  Pretty common occurrence on all types of cars. It is either a slipping belt, or early indication of water pump or alternator bearing failure. If you just adjusted the belt by the manual, try some belt dressing. If the noise goes away, don't worry about it. If it doesn't, remove the belt and see if you can wiggle the pulley on either the pump or alternator. Also, with light pressure, try spinning them by hand and see if they turn smooth or if they bind up a little. Also, I forgot to mention, if you put the belt on too tight, it can lead to premature bearing failure. Hope this helps.<p>[This message has been edited by kidzwheelz (edited 02-10-2000).]||||reg||1
